 "standard_url": "https://nerdc.gov.ng/",
 "standard_text": "Use directed numbers on a number line; add and subtract positive and negative numbers; solve problems with temperature and money. (summary of the NERDC JSS 1 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 1 maths worksheets on directed numbers: the number line, adding and subtracting positive and negative numbers, and problems with temperature and height. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Subtracting a negative = adding",
 "key_sub": "−3 + 5 = 2",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Numbers to the right on the number line are bigger: −2 &gt; −7.</li><li>Adding a positive number moves right; adding a negative number moves left.</li><li>Subtracting a negative number is the same as adding: 4 − (−3) = 4 + 3 = 7.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>−8 + 3</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Start at −8, move 3 right</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: −5</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>−2 − (−6)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>−2 + 6</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 4</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Thinking −7 &gt; −2</td><td>−7 is further left, so it is smaller.</td></tr><tr><td>Subtracting a negative as subtracting</td><td>Two minus signs together make plus.</td></tr><tr><td>Losing the sign</td><td>Write the sign in the answer.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What are directed numbers?",
   "a": "Numbers with a sign, + or −, that show a direction."
  },
  {
   "q": "Where do we see negative numbers?",
   "a": "Temperatures below zero, debts and depths below sea level."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is −5 + 5?",
   "a": "0."
  }
 ],
